{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "mom6_cgrid_flux_ppm",
  "description": "Numeric conformance problem for the mom6_cgrid PPM flux/divergence rules (grids/mom6_cgrid/rules/mom6_cgrid_flux_x/y.esm and mom6_cgrid_div_x/y.esm) on a tiny 7x7x1 grid (the grid metaparameters N_I/N_J/N_K are bound to 7/7/1 by the simulation manifest; 7 is the smallest size on which every pinned face (i,j in [3, N-2]) carries the full 6-cell PPM reconstruction stencil) by the simulation manifest): the same five equations as the consuming EqESM model \u2014 the zonal/meridional PPM layer fluxes uh = mom6_cgrid_flux_x(h, u_E, dy_Cu_E, mask, h_min_recon, dt, IdxT, IdxT_e) and vh = mom6_cgrid_flux_y(h, v_N, dx_Cv_N, mask, h_min_recon, dt, IdyT, IdyT_n) (zonal_flux_layer / merid_flux_layer, MOM_continuity_PPM.F90:933-956 / 1809-1893, with the PPM_reconstruction_x/y parabolas F90:2327-2478 / 2503-2629 and the PPM_limit_pos limiter F90:2636-2674 built from the stencil laws), the C-grid face-flux divergences div_x = D(uh,x), div_y = D(vh,y), and the continuity PDE D(h,t) = -(div_x + div_y).  The hand-chosen state exercises every branch of the flux laws at once: u_E > 0 at the (3,3) face, u_E < 0 at (4,4), u_E > 0 at (3,4) whose west neighbour cell (2,4) is MASKED (mask = 0, exercising the masked-slope zeroing and the masked-neighbour edge replacement), v_N < 0 at (3,3), v_N > 0 at (4,4) and (3,4), zero velocities elsewhere, and the zero-flux EAST and NORTH wall regions (faces i = 7 and j = 7) of the flux rules' explicit wall regions.  The 14 expected values are the MOM6 laws evaluated by the independent Python transcription of stage1/analysis/extract_mom6_dyn_test.py (EqESM), which reproduces the instrumented Fortran's uh_E/uh_W/vh_N/vh_S columns at rel 1e-12; the rule lowering agrees with the Fortran at rel 1e-12 (EqESM stage2/mom6_dynamics.esm pins), so the two independent transcriptions of the same law bound the golden at rel 1e-11 (the rule groups dy*(u*(...)) where the Fortran/Python group (dy*u)*(...), leaving a few ULPs of association-order slack; the AST fixture tests/conformance/ast/mom6_cgrid_continuity pins the byte-identical expansion).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "conformance",
   "problem",
   "grid:mom6_cgrid",
   "rule:mom6_cgrid_flux_x",
   "rule:mom6_cgrid_flux_y",
   "rule:mom6_cgrid_div_x",
   "rule:mom6_cgrid_div_y"
  ]
 },
 "models": {
  "Mom6CgridFluxPpm": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "../grids/mom6_cgrid/grid.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/mom6_cgrid/rules/mom6_cgrid_flux_x.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/mom6_cgrid/rules/mom6_cgrid_flux_y.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/mom6_cgrid/rules/mom6_cgrid_div_x.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/mom6_cgrid/rules/mom6_cgrid_div_y.esm"
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "h": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Layer thickness on the T cells, the continuity state (a hand-chosen 6x6 bump profile in [1, 2.4] m with one masked cell at (2,4))."
    },
    "uh": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Zonal layer volume flux at the east faces, the flux_x rule target."
    },
    "vh": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Meridional layer volume flux at the north faces, the flux_y rule target."
    },
    "div_x": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Zonal face-flux divergence, the div_x rule target."
    },
    "div_y": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Meridional face-flux divergence, the div_y rule target."
    },
    "u_E": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "East-face zonal velocity of the C-grid staggering (nonzero at the (3,3), (4,4) and (3,4) faces)."
    },
    "v_N": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "k"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "North-face meridional velocity of the C-grid staggering (nonzero at the (3,3), (4,4) and (3,4) faces)."
    },
    "dy_Cu_E": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Length of the east face (uniform 1 m on the tiny grid)."
    },
    "dx_Cv_N": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Length of the north face (uniform 1 m on the tiny grid)."
    },
    "mask": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "0/1 ocean-cell indicator (all 1 except the masked cell (2,4))."
    },
    "IdxT": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "1/m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "1/dxT of the cell (uniform 0.1 1/m on the tiny grid's 10 m cells)."
    },
    "IdxT_e": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "1/m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "1/dxT of the east neighbour cell, the u_E < 0 branch CFL denominator."
    },
    "IdyT": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "1/m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "1/dyT of the cell (uniform 0.1 1/m)."
    },
    "IdyT_n": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "1/m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "1/dyT of the north neighbour cell, the v_N < 0 branch CFL denominator."
    },
    "IareaT": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "1/m^2",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "1/cell area (uniform 0.01 1/m^2 on the 10 m x 10 m cells), the divergence rules' free-name contract with the grid."
    },
    "h_min_recon": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "The PPM_limit_pos thickness floor (1e-10 m)."
    },
    "dt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "The tracer time step (100 s; CFL = |u|*dt*IdxT = 0.2 at the 0.02 m/s faces)."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "uh",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "mom6_cgrid_flux_x",
      "args": [
       "h",
       "u_E",
       "dy_Cu_E",
       "mask",
       "h_min_recon",
       "dt",
       "IdxT",
       "IdxT_e"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vh",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "mom6_cgrid_flux_y",
      "args": [
       "h",
       "v_N",
       "dx_Cv_N",
       "mask",
       "h_min_recon",
       "dt",
       "IdyT",
       "IdyT_n"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "div_x",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "uh"
      ],
      "wrt": "x"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "div_y",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "vh"
      ],
      "wrt": "y"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "h"
      ],
      "wrt": "t"
     },
     "rhs": {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "div_x",
         "div_y"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "flux_law_numeric",
     "description": "Instantaneous numeric pin (time span 0 to 0, rel 1e-11) of the rule-lowered fluxes, divergences and wall regions on the tiny 7x7x1 grid. The 7x7 grid is the smallest on which every pinned face (i,j in [3, N-2]) carries the full 6-cell PPM stencil. The test state is the hand-chosen field of the metadata description: h the 6x6 bump profile with the masked cell (2,4), u_E/v_N nonzero at the (3,3) (+/- branches), (4,4) (-/+ branches) and (3,4) (+, with the masked west neighbour) faces, uniform metrics (10 m cells: IdxT/IdxT_e/IdyT/IdyT_n = 0.1 1/m, dy_Cu_E/dx_Cv_N = 1 m, IareaT = 0.01 1/m^2), dt = 100 s, h_min_recon = 1e-10 m. The expected values are the MOM6 laws evaluated by the independent Python transcription of the EqESM dump extractor (reproduces the Fortran columns at rel 1e-12); the tolerance rel 1e-11 covers the association-order slack between the rule lowering and the Python evaluation (each is within rel 1e-12 of the Fortran; the rule groups dy*(u*(...)) where the Fortran groups (dy*u)*(...)). The uh(7,3) and vh(3,7) assertions pin the explicit zero-flux east/north wall regions of the flux rules.",
